ained flat with mechanic and repair  trades dropping nearly eight percent  Precision production dropping 10 percent  and construction trades Rising just  minimally so there's significant  problems that and and every every year  that problem doesn't get better it gets  worse because there's more people  leaving the trades and getting into the  trades this amid record high labor  demand and an increase of the Baby  Boomers aging into retirement the  numbers a stark difference from the  amount of working age Canadians with a  bachelor's degree or higher that Rose  more than 19 percent according to the  census something industry experts say  needs to be addressed at a Grassroots  level instruction is not being presented  as a career of choice high schoolers are  not necessarily getting that balanced  message about what you can do in  construction which can do in trades the  report also indicates trades have been  limited by an underrepresentation of  women immigrants and racialized groups  as well as a high unemployment rate  among immigrants with foreign degrees  something that Canadian construction  Association says needs to be addressed  but until then the lack of laborers  means a service slowdown back in the  shop we're currently booking first week  of January other shops I heard are  booking into March so it's anywhere from  five to eight weeks 12 weeks now it's an  issue that isn't new but likely one that  isn't going anywhere anytime soon  statscan says the trend is expected to  continue over the next decade as more  baby boomers reach retirement now to put  that into perspective in 2021 30 percent  of workers in mechanic or Precision  production trades were over the age of  55. Marty blunt Global News Ottawa  cattle chaos next The Runaway cows  creating headaches for Quebec farmers  [Music]  [Music]  [Applause]  Applause for the baguette the crunchy  quintessentially French bread has been  added to the United Nations cultural  heritage list the country is said 